{
  "_doc": "Operational-role taxonomy. backend/util/roles.py loads this lazily on first use (not at import), so a late FLY_DATA_DIR is honoured. The frontend gets role/group data from role_catalog.json (fetched at runtime by frontend/src/data.js), which backend/pipeline/etl/publish/export.py builds by reading this file via backend.util.roles.taxonomy(). Adding/changing a designator's role is a JSON edit, not a code change. `groups` is the single source of truth for the published UI group table (order, slug, label, default on-flag, member role slugs); export.py's role_catalog builder reads it via taxonomy()['groups'] rather than defining its own copy. The three pseudo-roles in the 'role_unknown' group (typecode_unknown, type_unknown, role_unknown) are synthetic — they do not appear in the 'roles' map above, only as bucket labels for unresolved aircraft.",
